    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1755">

                <pb facs="1423" n="1307" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.0145/14.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 313.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 19, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence on
                    the subject of the extension of the area of territorial waters to twelve miles
                    by the Russian Government, I have the honor to enclose herewith a copy of a note
                    which I have been able to procure—a note from the Russian Imperial Ministry of
                    Foreign Affairs in reply to the protest entered by Japan against this extension
                    in the Pacific Ocean. While this note is not of recent date, having been sent to
                    the Japanese Embassy a year ago last March, it may prove of interest to the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles S. Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d1755-a1.xml" xpointer="d1755-a1"/>
            </div>
